course: dictionary
lesson: 1513
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Mix the cement with water and sand.» Here cement is a grey powder. «The win cemented her place in the team.» Here cement is a verb, meaning to make something stronger or more certain.
explain: Check the clues around the word. Ask: is it a thing or an action? In «A cement mixer lorry keeps its drum turning», cement mixer names a machine, so cement is a thing. In «Sandstone is made of sand grains cemented together», the -ed ending shows an action that has already happened.
explain: Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one fits. Could you cement a friendship? Yes, so the verb works there. If you are still stuck, a dictionary lists every meaning, so you can check which one fits best.
fact: Cement can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: As a noun, cement is a grey powder mixed with water, sand and stones to make concrete or mortar.
fact: «Sandstone» is made of sand grains «cemented together», often from old beaches, rivers or deserts.
fact: «Concrete» sets because of a chemical reaction with water, not just because it dries.
fact: Wet cement can burn skin, so keep it off your hands.
exercise: «A cement mixer lorry keeps its drum turning so the concrete does not set.» What is a cement mixer? | A kind of cake | A glue for paper | A boat for carrying sand | *A lorry that keeps concrete mixed so it does not set
exercise: «The win cemented her place in the team.» What does cemented mean here? | Painted a sign | Stuck in mud | Broke in two | *Made her place more certain
exercise: In «Sandstone is made of sand grains cemented together», what kind of word is cemented? | A question word | A name for a place | A noun, naming a thing | *A verb, showing an action
test: «Conglomerate is a rock made of rounded pebbles, cemented together.» What does cemented mean here? | *Stuck together | Broken into dust | Washed away by the sea | Painted red
test: Nadia says cement only means grey powder. What is the best answer? | Yes, it only ever means grey powder | It means a grey sky | It means a kind of rock | *It can also be a strong glue or a verb meaning to make something more certain
exam: Which sentence uses cement as a verb? | «Wet cement can burn skin.» | *«The children cemented their friendship with a secret handshake.» | «Mix the cement with water and sand.» | «A cement mixer lorry is parked outside.»
